.TH REDUMPER-GUI 1 "2026-07-12" "redumper-gui v1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redumper-gui \- desktop frontend for the redumper optical-disc dumper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redumper-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B redumper-gui
is a graphical frontend for
.BR redumper (1),
the low-level disc dumper used by the Redump preservation project. It
enumerates the optical drives on the system, runs a dump, streams
redumper's log into the window, and afterwards compresses the log files
and packs them into a submission-ready ZIP.
.PP
It takes no command-line options; everything is configured in the window.
.SH DUMPER VERSION
The GUI is coupled to a specific redumper build: upstream bundles one and
states that other versions may not be supported. This package therefore
depends on
.BR redumper-rgui ,
a compatibility package carrying exactly that build, and invokes it
directly \(em not whatever
.B redumper
happens to be on
.BR PATH .
The rolling
.B redumper
package can be installed at the same time and is the one to use on the
command line; the two do not conflict.
.SH MPF POST-PROCESSING
If the
.B mpf-check
package is installed, the GUI runs MPF.Check on the finished dump to
produce Redump submission info. It is a weak dependency: without it the
dump still completes and the post-processing step is simply skipped.
.SH DRIVE ACCESS
No root and no group membership are needed at a local desktop seat:
.BR systemd\-logind (8)
puts a
.B uaccess
ACL on the optical device node for the logged-in user, and the dumper
binary carries the
.B cap_sys_rawio
file capability for vendor SCSI passthrough. Headless, SSH and cron
sessions have no seat and therefore no ACL \(em they need the
.B cdrom
group or root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/redumper-gui/
Window layout and settings, written by the GUI.
.TP
.I redumper
Inside the GUI's private program directory: a symlink to the pinned dumper
the GUI executes. A second symlink,
.IR MPF.Check ,
points at the MPF validator and dangles harmlessly while
.B mpf-check
is not installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR redumper (1),
.BR mpf-check (1),
.BR mpf-gui (1)
.SH NOTES
This manpage is written and maintained by the packager; upstream ships none,
and the GUI takes no command-line options, so there is no
.B \-\-help
output a generator could work from.
.PP
The version in the header is therefore
.B deliberately static:
it records the release this text was written against
.RB ( v1.0.1 ),
not the version you have installed. Stamping the shipped version into a
hand-written page would be a forgery \(em the header would keep claiming
currency while the prose quietly aged. If your installed
.B redumper-gui
is newer than the version named above, treat this page as possibly behind.
